    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QywEtdgW7Sm1"
      },
      "source": [
        "Python follows the **LEGB** Rule\n",
        "\n",
        "* Local (L): Names assigned in any way within a function (def or lambda)), and not declared global in that function.\n",
        "* Enclosing (E) function locals: Name in the local scope of any and all enclosing functions (def or lambda), from inner to outer.\n",
        "* Global (G) module: Names assigned at the top-level of a module file, or declared global in a def within the file.\n",
        "* Built-in (B) Python: Names preassigned in the built-in names module : open, range, SyntaxError,..."
